            "full_final_body": "To find the total length of the path, we need to calculate the lengths of the vertical segments and the horizontal circular arcs separately and then sum them up.\n\n**1. Vertical Segments:**\nThe path is described as moving from the base to the top. The total height of the cylinder is given as $15 \\text{ cm}$. The vertical segments are the parts of the path that contribute to the upward movement. By adding the lengths of all the vertical segments together, the total vertical distance covered must equal the total height of the cylinder.\n*   **Total Vertical Length = $15 \\text{ cm}$**\n\n**2. Horizontal Circular Arcs:**\nThe horizontal segments are circular arcs along the surface of the cylinder. Let's analyze each one shown in the diagram:\n*   **First Arc (Red):** The path starts at $A$ and goes up to the first level. It then moves horizontally. The arc starts at the front (solid line) and goes to the back (dashed line), ending at the vertical generator (dashed line) that runs along the back. This represents half of a circle.\n*   **Second Arc (Blue):** The path goes up and then moves horizontally again. This arc starts from the back (dashed line) and comes to the front (solid line). It covers the other half of the circle to return to the front.\n    *   The sum of the first and second arcs is one full circle. Circumference $C = 30 \\text{ cm}$.\n*   **Third Arc (Red):** The path goes up and moves horizontally again. Similar to the first arc, it goes from the front (solid) to the back (dashed). This is another half-circle ($15 \\text{ cm}$).\n*   **Fourth Arc (Blue):** Finally, the path goes up to the top and moves horizontally to point $B$. The diagram shows this arc starting at the back (dashed) and ending at point $B$ in the front (solid). This completes the circle, returning to the front. This is the final half-circle ($15 \\text{ cm}$).\n\nSumming the horizontal arcs:\n*   Two half-circles on the front-to-back paths = $15 + 15 = 30 \\text{ cm}$.\n*   Two half-circles on the back-to-front paths = $15 + 15 = 30 \\text{ cm}$.\n*   **Total Horizontal Length = $30 + 30 = 60 \\text{ cm}$**\n\n**3. Total Length:**\nAdd the vertical and horizontal lengths together.\n$$ \\text{Total Length} = \\text{Vertical Length} + \\text{Horizontal Length} $$\n$$ \\text{Total Length} = 15 \\text{ cm} + 60 \\text{ cm} = 75 \\text{ cm} $$\n\nComparing this result to the choices:\nA: $45 \\mathrm{~cm}$\nB: $55 \\mathrm{~cm}$\nC: $60 \\mathrm{~cm}$\nD: $65 \\mathrm{~cm}$\nE: $75 \\mathrm{~cm}$\n\nThe correct choice is **E**.\n\n**Final Answer:**\nThe total length of the path is **75 cm**.",
